TypeScriptcURL <p>The SDK's iterators follow cursors for you:</p> <pre><code>for await (const p of permio.listPermissions({ pageSize: 50 })) {
  console.log(p.name);
}
</code></pre> <p>For other list RPCs, use <code>paginate</code> (see Listing with iterators).</p> <pre><code># First page
curl "$PERMIO_API/permissions-service/v1/permissions?project_name=default&amp;pagination.limit=50" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $PERMIO_API_KEY"

# Next page: pass the nextCursor value from the previous response
curl "$PERMIO_API/permissions-service/v1/permissions?project_name=default&amp;pagination.limit=50&amp;pagination.cursor=NEXT_CURSOR" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $PERMIO_API_KEY"
</code></pre> <p>Responses use camelCase JSON names, so the cursor arrives as <code>pagination.nextCursor</code>. When there are no more pages it is empty or left out.</p>

Option Type Default Description <code>apiKey</code> <code>string</code> required A <code>perms_…</code> key from the dashboard, or a legacy JWT key. <code>baseUrl</code> <code>string</code> <code>https://api.perms.io</code> API host. <code>DEV_BASE_URL</code> (<code>https://dev-api.perms.io</code>) is exported for the development API. <code>project</code> <code>string</code> none Default project name for <code>check*</code> and <code>list*</code> helpers. Each call can override it. <code>timeoutMs</code> <code>number</code> <code>10000</code> Timeout for each attempt, in ms. <code>0</code> disables it. <code>retries</code> <code>number \| RetryOptions</code> <code>2</code> Retries for idempotent reads. A number sets <code>maxRetries</code>; see Retries and timeouts. <code>fetch</code> <code>typeof fetch</code> <code>globalThis.fetch</code> Custom <code>fetch</code>, for example to add an agent, or for tests. <code>transport</code> <code>Transport</code> gRPC-web Advanced: a Connect transport to use instead, for example <code>createRouterTransport</code> in tests. <code>baseUrl</code> and <code>fetch</code> are then ignored. <p>The production default is <code>https://api.perms.io</code>. Versions 0.2.1 and earlier default to <code>https://temp-api.perms.io</code>, which is being retired: upgrade, or set <code>baseUrl</code>.</p> <pre><code>import { Permio, DEV_BASE_URL } from "permio";

const devClient = new Permio({ apiKey: process.env.PERMIO_API_KEY!, baseUrl: DEV_BASE_URL, project: "default" });
</code></pre> <p>The client also exposes <code>permio.project</code>, <code>permio.baseUrl</code> and <code>permio.apiKeyKind</code> (<code>"opaque"</code> or <code>"jwt"</code>).</p>
